Track: Wadud Game-Theoretic Baseline (AM / NSWF / EG)

New conductor track (wadud-baseline_20261101) to implement and evaluate the
baselines from Wadud, Golpayegani & Afraz, 2311.13389v1, against the existing
QACM CMC.

Why this paper: it is the direct precursor to QACM and the baseline QACM
itself benchmarks against. It uses the same substrate as our testbed
(polynomial surrogates over synthetic Gaussian KPI surfaces, one shared ICP,
per-conflict MNO priority weights) and needs no simulator or training loop.
It is therefore the highest-fidelity external comparison available.

Spec highlights:
- Metrics M1-M13: p*, per-xApp utility u_i, regret du_i, EG welfare and NSWF
  product, worst-off utility, utility spread, QoS satisfaction count (QACM
  extension), weighted QoS deviation, concession distance, latency,
  determinism.
- Scenarios S1-S9: direct (non-priority + priority), indirect, implicit,
  four-way scaling, synthetic out-of-sample pair/trio, weight sweep, and
  edge cases (zero utility, constant KPI, single xApp, zero weights).
- Reproduction targets from 2311.13389v1 section 5 with explicit tolerance
  and a mandatory discrepancy_reason when the published p* is not matched.
- Documented deviations: min-objective utility inversion, NSWF log-space
  epsilon clamp, EG solved by grid scan rather than an LP, and an open
  question on dataset provenance (data/QACM data1-5 mapping).

Plan: 4 phases (data provenance/utility -> baselines -> scenario matrix and
harness -> reporting/docs) with TDD tasks and checkpoints.

